  "title": "Deployments still suck, but maybe they don’t have to",
  "summary": "Deployments have come a long way, but still kinda suck. AWS makes simple things complicated. PaaS was the answer, until edge cases broke it. Now we’re stuck gluing together a dozen tools across a dozen dashboards. The future? One opinionated, flexible platform that just works.",
